// Declaration emit for the public subpath exports — `@taskless/cli/prompts`
// and `@taskless/cli/layout` — and nothing else.
//
// Vite's lib build emits JavaScript and no types, so `tsc` supplies the `.d.ts`
// for the entries that are public importable API. The include list is
// deliberately just those entries (plus the ambient build defines they need)
// rather than all of `src`: emitting a `dist/index.d.ts` next to `dist/index.js`
// would give the CLI's main entry a typed public surface it does not have today
// and has never promised, purely as a side effect of typing the new one.
//
// The include list bounds which entries are rooted here, not how many files are
// emitted. Declaration emit follows the import graph, so the modules the entry
// reaches get one too: `prompts/recipes`, `util/invocation`, and the two leaf
// Zod schemas. They ship in the tarball under `files: ["dist"]` but no `exports`
// condition points at them, so they stay reachable only as the types this
// entry's own signatures reference. `dist/index.d.ts` — the thing this scoping
// exists to prevent — is absent, which `test/prompts.test.ts` asserts.
//
// `declarationDir` is `dist` rather than following `TASKLESS_BUILD_TARGET` the
// way `vite.config.ts`'s `resolveOutDir()` does, because these exports resolve
// to `./dist/<entry>.js` unconditionally. The `self` target exists to
// run the CLI binary from a local path, and nothing resolves a prompts entry out
// of `dist-self`. Wiring this step into that build means overriding
// `--declarationDir` to match, or the declarations land beside the wrong
// JavaScript.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": false,
    "emitDeclarationOnly": true,
    "sourceMap": false,
    "rootDir": "src",
    "declarationDir": "dist"
  },
  "include": ["src/globals.d.ts", "src/prompts/index.ts", "src/layout/index.ts"]
}
